WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.420
Nigerian dishes that taste the same every time.

2
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:12.670
This is the video for Module 2 of Advanced Cooking and Nutrition: Nigerian and West African cuisine at a professional standard.

3
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:21.320
Ask ten cooks how they make stew and you get ten answers. In a business, that means Tuesday's stew is sweeter than Monday's.

4
00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:32.680
Professional kitchens use a standard recipe: the same ingredients, the same weights, the same method, every time. A kitchen scale is the most important tool.

5
00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.770
You will also cook rice, acha and beans with tested ratios.

6
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.010
And you will plate food so it looks as good as it tastes.

7
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:53.200
Fresh tomatoes are roughly 94% water. Step one. Blend your tomatoes, tatashe, which is red bell pepper, scotch bonnet and onion.

8
00:00:54.450 --> 00:01:05.800
Step two. Boil the blend uncovered until much of the water has gone. The common mistake is pouring it straight into hot oil. The oil spits and the stew can taste sour and raw.

9
00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.630
Step three. Fry the thick paste in oil.

10
00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:17.300
Keep frying until the oil separates and rises to the top. That sign means the water has cooked out.

11
00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:27.510
Then add stock and protein, taste, and adjust in small steps. Season lightly at the start, because flavour concentrates as it reduces.

12
00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:42.290
Here is a worked example. Ngozi blends 7.5 kg of tomatoes, peppers and onions, boils it down by half, and fries it until the oil rises. Her finished base weighs 4 kg.

13
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:46.160
Her tomatoes cost about 12,000 naira.

14
00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:54.600
Tatashe about 4,000 naira, scotch bonnet about 2,000, and onions about 2,500.

15
00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:59.630
Oil and seasoning add about 2,500 naira.

16
00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:12.850
The total is about 23,000 naira. At 120 g per plate, 4 kg gives 33 portions, so each plate carries about 697 naira of stew.

17
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:25.230
Parboiled rice usually needs about 1.5 to 2 cups of water per cup of rice. Brands differ, so test once and write down what works for your rice and your pot.

18
00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:32.240
Sort beans, then soak them for 6 to 8 hours or overnight. They cook faster and save gas.

19
00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:38.550
Throw away the soaking water. Some of the sugars that cause bloating dissolve into it.

20
00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:55.650
For example, Amina in Abuja cooked 1 kg of dry beans and got 2.4 kg. For 60 portions of 250 g, she divides 15,000 g by 2.4 and buys 7 kg with a small margin.

21
00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:07.390
Cereals are low in lysine and beans are low in methionine. Eaten together, like rice and beans or moi moi with pap, they give better quality protein.

22
00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:21.890
NAFDAC has warned against using pesticides such as dichlorvos to preserve food. Buy beans from sellers you trust, reject any with a chemical smell or powdery residue, and wash and soak them well.

23
00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:35.110
Bleaching palm oil gives heavy smoke and breaks down the oil. If you do it, use a small quantity, moderate heat, stay with the pot, open doors and windows, and never let it catch fire.

24
00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:46.580
Plating means a lot of contact with ready-to-eat food. Wash your hands, use tongs and spoons, and change gloves if you touch money, phones or your face.

25
00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:56.510
Think of the plate as a clock face. Protein at the front, starch at the back left and vegetables at the back right. Same layout every time.

26
00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:03.860
Brown next to brown looks dull. Add something green or bright, like cucumber or fried plantain.

27
00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:09.120
Shape rice in a bowl or ring mould and lean the protein against it.

28
00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:16.370
Leave the rim empty and wipe drips. Spoon stew next to the protein, so the rice stays white.

29
00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:25.640
Weigh what each ladle holds and write it on tape on the handle. Then every customer gets the same amount, and your costing stays true.

30
00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:37.210
To remember. Weigh everything and write it on a recipe card. Boil down the blend and fry until the oil rises. Add leafy vegetables last so they stay green.

31
00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:44.600
Test your yields and water ratios. And plate with a fixed layout, clean rims and garnish that belongs to the dish.

32
00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:55.730
Your practice: write a standard recipe and ask someone else to cook from it, build your yield page for rice and beans, and design and photograph a model plate.

33
00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.020
Continue with the lessons below.
